# Frontend UI state (MyWallet)

## Where logic lives

| Concern | Place |
|---------|-------|
| Auth session | Laravel + Inertia shared `auth` props |
| Forms / mutations | Inertia `useForm` / `router` in Pages |
| Pure format / enums | `resources/js/domain/` |
| Theme toggle | `infrastructure/` + thin Page/Layout callback |
| Reusable UI | `Components/` — props + booleans + callbacks only |

Do not add `useMemo` / `useCallback` equivalents by default (Vue computed/watch only when needed).

## No magic status strings in templates

Prefer named maps/enums from `domain/` (`WalletType`, `TxType`) over raw string compares scattered in templates.

```vue
<!-- ❌ v-if="wallet.type === 'credit_card'" without shared constant -->
<!-- ✅ use WalletType.CreditCard or label from WALLET_TYPE_LABELS -->
```

## Components

- Presentational: data + named booleans + callbacks.
- Lists: stable `:key="item.id"`.
- Catch as `unknown` then narrow — no `any`.

## Forbidden

- Inline magic status strings when a domain enum/map exists
- God SFCs (~200+ lines): split shell / list / form sections
- Hiding HTTP/fetch inside presentational Components
